  abstract={This paper presents a trustworthy agentic AI frame-work for resilient IoT security operations that addresses challenges in detection, response, and policy-aware defense in distributed IoT environments. The rapid expansion of the Internet of Things (IoT) ecosystems have significantly increased the cyberattack surface, creating complex challenges for operational security and organizational governance. Traditional detection-focused solutions are insufficient for real-world IoT environments, which demand autonomous, adaptive, and policy-aware defense mechanisms.The proposed framework integrates operational responses with organizational policy enforcement through edge-deployed AI agents that continuously monitor device behavior, network traffic, and system events. It incorporates graph-based IoT topology modeling to capture relationships among devices, anomaly detection modules to identify abnormal patterns, and adaptive decision-making mechanisms to enable context-aware mitigation actions, including traffic isolation, access control adjustments, and resource prioritization.Trustworthiness is achieved through robustness against adversarial manipulation, reliability-aware action selection, and transparent logging to support auditability. The framework balances autonomous decision-making with adherence to organizational security policies, enabling real-time responses aligned with governance objectives.Evaluation on realistic IoT datasets demonstrates that the proposed framework achieves 95% detection accuracy and a 0.93 F1-score, outperforming traditional intrusion detection systems and standalone machine learning models while reducing detection time and enabling real-time response. These results highlight its effectiveness in improving resilience, operational efficiency, and policy compliance in complex IoT environments.},
