  abstract={Many algorithms are evolved for security to prevent attacks and some simulated real traffic as dataset and some considered the bench mark datasets like NSL-KDD, CIC-IDS, BoT-IoT, ROUT-4-2023, UNSW-NB15, KDD cup 1999, Edge-IIoT and these are the some of the datasets previously investigated for intrusion detection system as well as intrusion prevention by working on various machine learning algorithms such as Random forest (RF), SVM Support vector machines algorithm, KNN algorithms like K-means, K-medoids and various deep learning algorithms such as XGBoost, Even though there are research gaps in terms of detecting the attacks, model complexity, evaluation of model and class balancing issues. In this paper, proposing a new algorithm to design a model that can solve the above gaps and trying to fulfil the research ethics. The model Ultra-Regularized deep neural network for IoT classification (URDNN-IoT) in deep learning and testing on ROUT-4-2023 dataset and achieved the accuracy of 99.264%, 99.273 precision, 99.264 recall and F1 score as 99.273 on early stopping and balanced and stable accuracy and loss curves are displayed. This model is using deep architecture good for complex patterns, funnel structure for gradual width reduction, BatchNorm stabilizing the training phase, and performing both binary and multiclass classification with Softmax. Comparing to the base line models such as RaD-FFNN (95%), ANF-TBR (60%), FL-based IDS (91%), Temporal CNN (97%), the proposed model gave good accuracy and performance metrics are highly reliable and stable than compared to the existing baseline models.},
